Product Specifications: Why do you need this: For Reselling

Instructions:

Task 1: 
Product Specifications: Why do you need this: For Reselling Assessment:
    a) Spelling Error in Product Specifications: 
    Flag words that are contextually incorrect for an industrial listing.
    Flag only clear typos in common dictionary words (e.g., "Steel" vs "Stel").
    Guardrail: DO NOT flag brand names, model numbers (e.g., "L805", "GGT"), or unit concatenations (e.g., "70ltr", "20inch", "400kg.up"). These are standard in industrial listings.

b) Contradiction/ Redundancy in Product Specifications: Flag as "outlier" only if values are physically impossible to coexist (e.g., Material: Wood and Material: Stainless Steel). 
    (Conflicts within the Product Title itself do not infer or assume anything else.)

Task 2:
Specification Based Query: Generate a  query using Product Specifications. Maximum word limit 4. Query should be SEO friendly to be used in ecommerce search.

Task 3:
Category Analysis: Analyze the Category Name: FMCG Products and identify the type of products it represents.
Only flag as "outlier" if the entity does not belong in the category. Ignore spelling/formatting errors in the entities. Use the Category understanding from above to identify if there is a contradiction in:
    a) Product Specifications - Category Name

Task 4:
Product-Category Integrity Audit Analyze the Product Specifications against Category Name: FMCG Products to identify logical dissonance. Flag as "outlier" if any of the following gates fail:
    a) Entity State (Part vs. Machine): Mark as "outlier" if the Product Specifications represents a sub-component/spare (e.g., Nozzle, Valve) but the category is for a complete unit (e.g., Blasting Machine).
    b) Material Truth: Mark as "outlier" if the Product Specifications contradicts the category name (e.g., wooden texture visible for "SS Table", or plastic for "Metallic Gear").
    c) Hierarchy Mismatch: Flag as "outlier" if a finished product is placed in a "Raw Material" category (e.g., a finished bench in "Teak Wood Lumber") or if a physical product is placed in a "Service" category.
    d) Functional Alignment: Mark as "outlier" if the Product  utility is unrelated to the category's intended purpose.

Give all output in JSON format.
Give response for task and subtasks of task 1,  task 3 and task 4 as outlier / not outlier / can't say for each subtask. Give one reason for each subtask of task 1,  task 3 and task 4.

